 "feedback": "A reference implementation that meets the specification violates dout_after_read at DEPTH = 4, WIDTH = 8. Those properties are wrong, not the design. Counterexample (values just before each edge):\nedge | rst | wr_en | rd_en | din | dout | full | empty\n0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0\n1 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 128 | 0 | 0 | 1\n2 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0\n3 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 128 | 0 | 0\n4 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1\n5 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1\n6 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1\nCorrect or remove them and resubmit the whole set.",
 "frozen": {
